---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
const updated = 'June 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="How medicalbeforeaftergallery.com handles your data.">
  <section class="legal">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy explains how {site.legalName} (“we”, “us”) handles information when you visit
          <a href={site.url}>{site.domain}</a> (the “Site”). It applies to this marketing website only.
        </p>

        <h2>Information we collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Contact form.</strong> When you submit our contact form, we collect the name, email, topic and message you provide so we can respond. Submissions are delivered to us by our form provider, Web3Forms.</li>
          <li><strong>Analytics.</strong> We use Google Analytics to understand aggregate, anonymized traffic (pages viewed, approximate location, device/browser). This uses cookies.</li>
          <li><strong>Server logs.</strong> Our host (GitHub Pages) may process standard request data such as IP address for security and reliability.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How we use information</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>To respond to your enquiries and provide support.</li>
          <li>To measure and improve the Site’s content and performance.</li>
          <li>To keep the Site secure and operational.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Sharing</h2>
        <p>
          We do not sell your personal information. We share data only with the service providers that operate
          this Site — Google Analytics (analytics), Web3Forms (contact form delivery), and our checkout provider
          Freemius if you choose to purchase Pro. Each processes data under their own privacy terms.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          The Site uses analytics cookies. You can disable cookies in your browser settings; the Site will still
          function.
        </p>

        <h2>Patient data</h2>
        <p>
          This Site is for promoting our WordPress plugin. Please do not submit patient images or any protected
          health information (PHI) through the contact form. You are responsible for obtaining appropriate patient
          consent and complying with applicable privacy regulations when publishing before/after images on your
          own website.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on your location, you may have the right to access, correct or delete the personal information
          we hold about you. To make a request, use our <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about this policy? <a href="/contact/">Get in touch</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
  }
  .narrow {
    max-width: 760px;
  }
  .legal h1 {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }
  .updated {
    color: var(--text-light);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
</style>
